WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.109 --> 00:00:09.458
Jack stood with Hulk and Laura on the deck of the pool. The Sharks' swim meet against the Pacific Piranhas was about to start.

2
00:00:09.459 --> 00:00:18.776
Mrs. Wilson walked over to Hulk and spread her arms wide. "One last hug for my precious little Tommy."

3
00:00:18.777 --> 00:00:27.109
"You're the precious one, Grammy," Hulk said as they hugged. "You're the best grandmother in the whole wide world."

4
00:00:27.110 --> 00:00:32.783
"And you're the best grandson there ever was," Mrs. Wilson cooed.

5
00:00:32.784 --> 00:00:37.509
Laura nudged Jack and mimed throwing up.

6
00:00:37.510 --> 00:00:46.670
Jack laughed. Listening to Mrs. Wilson and Hulk was almost as nauseating as listening to the Long-Hair Boys.

7
00:00:46.671 --> 00:00:51.660
Still, he liked this version of Mrs. Wilson better than the cranky one.

8
00:00:51.661 --> 00:00:56.165
He wondered if her near-death experience had transformed her.

9
00:00:56.166 --> 00:01:01.677
Suddenly Mrs. Wilson spun toward Jack and jabbed her finger into his chest.

10
00:01:01.678 --> 00:01:06.069
"My little Tommy said you're swimming breaststroke on his relay team.

11
00:01:06.070 --> 00:01:10.075
You'd better not ruin his race, young man."

12
00:01:10.076 --> 00:01:18.060
"Yes, ma'am!" Jack said. Obviously, Mrs. Wilson's near-death experience hadn't changed her at all.

13
00:01:18.061 --> 00:01:29.978
As she made her way to the chairs alongside the pool, Jack muttered to Laura, "I'm still waiting to be thanked for that little favor—saving her life."

14
00:01:29.979 --> 00:01:36.462
Laura giggled. "Good luck with that," she said. "She'd rather yell at you."

15
00:01:36.463 --> 00:01:46.383
Just then the announcer lifted his megaphone. "The boys' two-hundred-meter medley relay will start in two minutes."

16
00:01:46.384 --> 00:01:53.606
Coach Shin patted Jack's back. "We need to win this," he said sternly.

17
00:01:53.607 --> 00:01:56.810
Jack shivered. He felt nervous.

18
00:01:56.811 --> 00:02:07.676
It would be horrible to perform poorly, especially after he and Hulk and Laura had spent so much effort convincing their coach to let him participate.

19
00:02:07.677 --> 00:02:14.786
But the kids on the Pacific Piranhas team were very good swimmers. It was going to be a challenging race.

20
00:02:14.787 --> 00:02:21.096
The starter blew a whistle, signaling the backstroke swimmers to get ready.

21
00:02:21.097 --> 00:02:27.682
"Good luck," Jack told his teammate Sebastian as Sebastian got into the water.

22
00:02:27.683 --> 00:02:32.847
"Good luck to you too. The four of us have to win this thing," Sebastian said.

23
00:02:32.848 --> 00:02:35.739
"But no pressure, right?" Jack joked.

24
00:02:35.740 --> 00:02:40.337
Sebastian frowned, obviously feeling a whole lot of pressure.

25
00:02:40.338 --> 00:02:43.955
The starter checked to make sure everyone was in position.

26
00:02:43.956 --> 00:02:52.898
Then a horn sounded, and the six backstroke specialists were off.

27
00:02:52.899 --> 00:02:56.729
Sebastian started quickly but lost steam.

28
00:02:56.730 --> 00:03:01.241
As he approached the far end of the pool, he was in the middle of the pack.

29
00:03:01.242 --> 00:03:08.145
He had paced himself poorly. At the turn Sebastian lost more time.

30
00:03:08.146 --> 00:03:15.303
Now he was stroking back toward Jack, but he was falling farther and farther behind.

31
00:03:15.304 --> 00:03:24.456
Jack's relay team would lose for sure unless Jack was one of the fastest breaststrokers in the pool. But Jack wasn't.

32
00:03:24.457 --> 00:03:31.639
He'd been a standout in Oklahoma, but he wasn't one here in California. He was going to lose his—

33
00:03:31.640 --> 00:03:36.945
"Focus, Jack!" he heard Mrs. Wilson shout, snapping him to attention.

34
00:03:36.946 --> 00:03:44.190
"Streamline the dive, cup your hands, and bring your head down far enough!"

35
00:03:44.191 --> 00:03:50.839
By the time Sebastian touched the wall and finished his fifty meters, Jack was totally focused.

36
00:03:50.840 --> 00:03:58.270
He dived into the water fast, making sure to keep his head down and his legs together.

37
00:03:58.271 --> 00:04:03.021
Yes! His dive was perfectly streamlined.

38
00:04:03.022 --> 00:04:07.027
Once Jack was in the water, he kept his body streamlined.

39
00:04:07.028 --> 00:04:11.912
He made sure his head wasn't too high, as Mrs. Wilson had kept telling him.

40
00:04:11.913 --> 00:04:17.488
His arms and legs were extended, with his fingers pointed ahead and his toes behind him.

41
00:04:17.489 --> 00:04:26.657
He swept out his arms. His head and chest exploded out of the water as he propelled his body forward.

42
00:04:26.658 --> 00:04:32.067
The real weapon in the breaststroke was the legs—and Jack's were strong.

43
00:04:32.068 --> 00:04:40.830
He bent them, bringing his heels up before pushing his legs out and to the sides in powerful kicks.

44
00:04:40.831 --> 00:04:48.140
An instant later Jack returned to the streamlined position. Then he started all the motions again.

45
00:04:48.141 --> 00:04:53.039
Jack got to the far end of the pool quickly, setting a good pace for the turn.

46
00:04:53.040 --> 00:05:00.725
He palmed the wall, pivoted, kicked off, and took off. Fantastic!

47
00:05:00.726 --> 00:05:08.788
He powered back to the other end of the pool and touched the wall. Phew! His leg of the race was over!

48
00:05:08.789 --> 00:05:13.953
As his teammate started the butterfly, Jack got out of the pool.

49
00:05:13.954 --> 00:05:20.697
"Good job, Jack! You got us from fifth place to third!" Sebastian cried.

50
00:05:20.698 --> 00:05:29.119
Jack nodded, but he was focused on the water. Laura was swimming the butterfly, the only girl competing in this relay.

51
00:05:29.120 --> 00:05:39.599
He felt so lucky to have her on his team. She wasn't just pretty. She was speedy, smoothly cutting through the water.

52
00:05:39.600 --> 00:05:43.619
She finished fast enough to get the team into second place.

53
00:05:43.620 --> 00:05:45.643
Their anchor was Hulk.

54
00:05:45.644 --> 00:05:53.773
His freestyle was not a pretty sight, unless you liked watching a gigantic machine tearing through the water like a chainsaw.

55
00:05:53.774 --> 00:06:00.835
But he got the job done. By the time he reached the turn, he was even with the fastest Pacific Piranhas swimmer.

56
00:06:00.836 --> 00:06:05.079
After the turn he was ahead.

57
00:06:05.080 --> 00:06:13.611
Before he even hit the wall to finish the race, Jack and Sebastian and Laura were jumping up and down.

58
00:06:13.612 --> 00:06:16.901
They'd won the relay!

59
00:06:16.902 --> 00:06:21.493
Once he'd finished his leg, Hulk tried to hug his teammates.

60
00:06:21.494 --> 00:06:29.731
Jack still had a slight bruise from the last time Hulk had hugged him. So he backed away, faking an urgent need for the bathroom.

61
00:06:29.732 --> 00:06:34.395
The rest of the meet wasn't as exciting for Jack as the relay race.

62
00:06:34.396 --> 00:06:39.639
He watched Hulk win the two-hundred-meter freestyle and individual medley races.

63
00:06:39.640 --> 00:06:45.630
He rooted for Laura as she won the girls' butterfly and came in third for the girls' backstroke.

64
00:06:45.631 --> 00:06:52.224
Jack got fifth place in the hundred-meter freestyle and third place in the hundred-meter breaststroke.

65
00:06:52.225 --> 00:06:56.554
Noah had told him he shouldn't complain about not being the best on the team.

66
00:06:56.555 --> 00:07:01.542
And Jack's father had said that being around fast swimmers would help him go faster.

67
00:07:01.543 --> 00:07:07.622
Still, Jack really liked to win. So he couldn't help feeling disappointed.

68
00:07:07.623 --> 00:07:12.864
The end of the meet was exciting though. That was when the winner was announced.

69
00:07:12.865 --> 00:07:17.354
The Sharks had beaten the Pacific Piranhas by two points.

70
00:07:17.355 --> 00:07:20.660
"Woo-hoo!" the Sharks cheered.

71
00:07:20.661 --> 00:07:26.505
Jack nudged Laura. "Is Coach Shin actually smiling?"

72
00:07:26.506 --> 00:07:33.766
"Hmm." Laura peered at their coach, grinning. "I think so, but it's definitely hard to tell."

73
00:07:33.767 --> 00:07:40.426
"Yay, Jack!" Luke screamed from where he was sitting with the boys' parents.

74
00:07:40.427 --> 00:07:44.497
"I'm so happy we won!" Laura exclaimed.

75
00:07:44.498 --> 00:07:48.172
They hugged—until a growl pulled them apart.

76
00:07:48.173 --> 00:07:57.078
"Laura and Jack," Mrs. Wilson snapped, "the pool deck is no place for a public display of affection!"

77
00:07:57.079 --> 00:08:05.968
Jack shook his head, laughing. "Thanks, Mrs. Wilson," he called, giving her a big wave.

78
00:08:05.969 --> 00:08:19.087
Hulk's precious grammy was difficult, but he was starting to get used to her—and everything else in California.

